# Community Web receipt chips (sig / intent)

`sig:…` and `intent://…` locators render as `button.cn-sig-text[data-receipt-locator]`.

## Do not regress

- Never leave these as bare native `<button>` chrome (UA gray fill, outset border).
- Never strip `.cn-sig-text` / `button.cn-sig-text` rules down to ellipsis-only.
- Required treatment (DESIGN.md `button-receipt` + Bracket Rule):
  - `appearance: none`, `background: none`, `border: 0`, `font: inherit`
  - `color: var(--cw-signed)`
  - `::before` / `::after` with `[` / `]`
  - focus-visible outline using `--cw-signed`

## When editing console CSS

Embedded CSS in `packages/Epoch.Community.Web/app/console.js` is the source of truth for board chrome. Large CSS rewrites often wipe receipt styles — after any CSS edit in that file, confirm `.cn-sig-text` still has the full Bracket Rule block.

## Gate

`npm run community-web:app:design-lint` (part of `gate:commit`) fails closed if receipt / Bracket Rule chrome is missing. Do not weaken or bypass that lint to land CSS changes.
